# Invitation request form (Netlify Forms + Netlify-provided reCAPTCHA)
# No local env vars are required for captcha in this flow.
# In Netlify UI, enable reCAPTCHA under Forms spam protection settings.

# Netlify Identity — only needed when the app is NOT served from your Netlify site
# (e.g. `next dev` on localhost). Point at your site’s Identity API:
# https://YOUR-SITE.netlify.app/.netlify/identity
# With `npx netlify dev`, leave unset so the widget uses the same origin.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_NETLIFY_IDENTITY_URL=

# --- Local Netlify DB (optional) ---
# In production, Netlify sets NETLIFY_DATABASE_URL when Netlify DB is linked.
# Paste a connection string from Neon (Netlify UI → Extensions → Neon) only here — never commit.
# If this URL was ever exposed, rotate the DB password in Neon and update Netlify + this file locally.
# npm run db:verify
# npm run db:apply-schema   (runs netlify/db/schema.sql once)
# Optional: run netlify/db/migration_content.sql if you created the DB before site_content / new meal columns existed.
# Optional: run netlify/db/seed-content.sql for default past menus + marketing JSON (key `site`).
# NETLIFY_DATABASE_URL=

# --- Netlify environment (set in Netlify UI only: Site → Environment variables) ---
# Never commit production secrets. Do not use NEXT_PUBLIC_ for these.
#
# Host-request notifications (Resend) — both required for email to send:
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxx
# RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=Supper Collective <hello@suppercollective.org>
#
# Admin inbox(es) for new membership request emails (comma-separated or single):
# ADMIN_NOTIFICATION_EMAILS=bowenhendy@gmail.com,juliebhendy@gmail.com
# ADMIN_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL=your-admin@example.com
#
# Required to send Netlify Identity invites when approving members:
# NETLIFY_IDENTITY_ADMIN_TOKEN=
#
# Optional: protect notify-waitlist stub
# ADMIN_NOTIFY_SECRET=
#
# --- Stripe (guest seat checkout) ---
# Production REQUIRES STRIPE_SECRET_KEY. Without it, payment endpoints return 503
# (no free "paid" seats). Demo/stub fulfillment is opt-in only:
#   ALLOW_DEMO_PAYMENTS=true
# and is hard-blocked when Netlify CONTEXT=production even if that flag is set.
#
# Create a RESTRICTED key (rk_test_... / rk_live_...) — not a full secret key (sk_...).
# Dashboard: https://dashboard.stripe.com/test/apikeys → Create restricted key
#
# Minimum permissions for Supper Collective server functions:
#   Checkout Sessions — Write (create-checkout)
#   Checkout Sessions — Read  (confirm-payment verifies session after redirect)
#
# Set the same vars in Netlify UI (Site → Environment variables) for production.
# Use test-mode keys until you are ready to go live, then create matching live-mode keys.
#
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=rk_test_xxxx
# ALLOW_DEMO_PAYMENTS=true
#
# Webhook signing secret from Stripe Dashboard → Developers → Webhooks.
# Endpoint URL: https://suppercollective.org/.netlify/functions/stripe-webhook
# Events: checkout.session.completed, checkout.session.expired
# For local testing: stripe listen --forward-to localhost:8888/.netlify/functions/stripe-webhook
#
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_xxxx
